{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1503979-how-do-you-play-exalted","id":1503979,"title":"How do you play Exalted?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-02-26T21:34:09-08:00","id":1503979,"title":"How do you play Exalted?","content":"Hi, I'm curious, do you play Ex3? Any of the previous editions,? ExEss? A homebrew version maybe?<br /> <br /> Me personally don't play anymore, I consider Ex3 to be overdesigned. I played both Ex1 and Ex2 in the past but not anymore. I tried Ex:Ess but, honestly, I found it a bit boring. Finally I made my own homebrew system to play Exalted, but still I lost motivation.<br /> <br /> Bonus Question: Do you think Exalted is still worth playing?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://fivefoldcomicstance.thecomicseries.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Join the Strife</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/90-gonzo","name":"Gonzo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar90_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"934"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-27T01:00:59-08:00","id":1503982,"title":"","content":"Well, I think the whole idea has its merits as a setting, and third edition adds actually a lot of systems that are really interesting and actually add and play well with the sort of epic contect this sort of game is supposed to help the players and GM feel. That with a lot of flawed or outright failed ideas, of course.<br /> <br /> We have played exalted through the years, first, second and now third edition First was outright simplistic and very broken in the gameplay-story integration. Second, it helped a bit with the charms... but had a complete mess of a combat system that outright did not work. Thiird has I think the best streamlined system in general (but not yet quite in combat) and very thematic character types. The whole supernal skill concept for solars in particular I think it's a master stroke, making you able to feel ike 'the best' in a particular field. The lunars feel a lot more shapeshifting, the dragonblooded a lot more 'elemental benders', and so on, than in the previous editions.<br /> <br /> Still, the combat idea with the withering and decisive sort of attack, barely works and is still a bother in melee... and just simply does not work as a concept for ranged combat.I have had to heavily adapt it so everything is decisive and withering is more a secondary system to actually prepare for 'super hits', for instance. Again, solar charm trees, while most are brilliant and make a lot more sense than before, things like craft are a complete unworkable mess that I just simply had to mutilate heavily so my craft oriented player could actually enjoy and make sense of it.<br /> <br /> In general, we are running this 3rd edition campaign and we are enjoying it... which is quite the target, but I feel that 3rd edition could have done with a pair more years of heavy polishing and play testing that it simply could not have.<br /> <br /> Essence I looked at and... oversimplified stuff is just not my thing as a GM.<br /> <br /> So in general... yes, but it demands a bit of an effort to make it work for you, if you want to actually enjoy the setting and the themes that I feel are pretty unique to this 'world'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3320-cathakjordi","name":"CathakJordi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3320_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-27T03:19:04-08:00","id":1503983,"title":"","content":"I'm not going to try 3E again - I spent far too much time trying to get it to work properly for me, before realizing it's not worth the effort when there are so many other workable systems out there. Likewise, I probably won't ever run Essence, as my understanding is that it sticks to a lot of the same mechanical concepts I didn't care for in 3E. The most likely way I'd actually touch Exalted mechanics again would be to go back to 2.5, but that's still really unlikely.<br /> <br /> That said, I still run stuff with the setting now and then, using Godbound or other easily adaptable rules. So, to the bonus question, I'd say the setting is definitely worth playing, but not the mechanics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2433-highpriest","name":"HighPriest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2433_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-27T03:43:08-08:00","id":1503984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gonzo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1503979-how-do-you-play-exalted#post1503979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi, I'm curious, do you play Ex3?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep. In two games at the moment.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Bonus Question: Do you think Exalted is still worth playing? </div> </div> </div>Well, considering I play it? Yes.<br /> <br /> My group prefers some of the house rules out there that I don't always like compared to the RAW or some other options, but nothing that's a deal breaker.<br /> <br /> That said, if Exalted is still owned by Paradox when it's finally time for 4e (or maybe a full 3.5e) so it still runs on the ST system, what I'd really love to see if Essence moved up to the core rules as the simplified version really does seem to suit how most people I know want to play the game for the most part, and then have the more complex 3e style subsystems available to add-on to fine-tune to the level of complexity your group wants.<br /> <br /> Essentially (no pun intended), all three core editions of Exalted have suffered one key flaw that's always plagued everything the game has tried to do: the core rules are written for normal humans and then have Exalted stuff slapped on top of them. While I enjoy a heroic mortal game personally, I think something Essence does right (and also something you see in things like Scion 2e) is that building the rules around playing super-powered beings from the get go makes everything easier to accomplish. I think that's why Godbound gets suggested so much (even if I think it's not really good at doing Exalted even if it's good at doing it's own version of epic fantasy RPG): Godbound is a game written for high powered demigods. By just tossing all the D&amp;D rules that only matter to mortal adventurers and focusing on the kinds of epic stories Godbound wants to do, it's a lot closer to what many Exalted fans have wanted for a long time. This is part of what makes the Cortex homebrew for Exalted one of the better ones in my mind: Cortex can run more simply like Godbound, while fairly seamlessly scaling up the mechanical complexity to Essence or even core Exalted levels. <br /> <br /> It's a heck of a lot easier to start with a simple version of the rules and then add to it, then trim things down later.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-27T03:56:21-08:00","id":1503985,"title":"","content":"I run two games of Ex3 which both employ slightly different house rules and tools to reflect the needs of the different groups.<br /> I run Pathfinder (not Exalted or set in Creation but a nice palate cleanser).<br /> I run Exalted Essence.<br /> I play in two more games which both run on Ex3.<br /> <br /> My experience is that it's mostly the game group, the community and to an extent the setting that I get attached to. The game system is often a secondary concern and needs to make my life very miserable for me to consider it the problem, but even then? I'd attribute most of my crap experiences with a system to fellow players who assumed because something was perfectly intuitive to them it was like that for everyone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 02-27-2023, 09:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-27T08:12:12-08:00","id":1503991,"title":"","content":"Last time I tried, I played with some new friends whose previous rpg experience was mainly 5e... It was almost impossible to make them understand the rules of Essence which were supposedly easier to get. They simply couldn't grasp the concept of two types of attacks. A total mess... My old Exalted table is disbanded, and I can't help but feel that the game in its current state is dead. News about new exalts getting their Kickstarter aren't exciting anymore. I kinda think &quot;damn.. six more years of this horrible horrible edition&quot;.<br /> <br /> And it's sad...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://fivefoldcomicstance.thecomicseries.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Join the Strife</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/90-gonzo","name":"Gonzo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar90_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"934"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-27T08:25:12-08:00","id":1503992,"title":"","content":"I run a bunch of Ex3 games in rotation (got about 6 or 7 in total, of which 3 are actively running atm). I make use of a smattering of homebrew content (additional Exalt types, Evocations, Martial Arts, Spells), but I wouldn't really call it a homebrew version.<br /> <br /> I theoretically still have an Ex2 game or two on the go, but its been... a while since we did anything with them.<br /> <br /> I've not had a chance to really look at ExEss yet - but I'm not as drawn to simpler mechanics so, I'm hesitant to really jump in there. Once I read it, we'll see how I take to it.<br /> <br /> Exalted is still worth playing, but only if you find the in-depth combat &amp; high-octane mechanics engaging. If you think of all that as busywork... then no.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>---------------------------------------------<br /> Supporter of Spirits getting full playable splat design come Exalted 3E.<br /> Refugee from the 3rd Great Edition Wars of D&amp;D. <br /> oWoD Latecomer, Exalted Optimist, Scion ST, Trinity Curious","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/955-yue-ryong","name":"Yue Ryong","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar955_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"147"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-02T19:48:47-08:00","id":1504240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gonzo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1503979-how-do-you-play-exalted#post1503979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi, I'm curious, do you play Ex3? Any of the previous editions,? ExEss? A homebrew version maybe?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> I had the utmost lucky finding one of the rare groups that play Exalted in Brasil. All the players in my group really really love the setting. I've never talked to them before and asked &quot;hey I really like Exalted, but I don't have a group... can I play with you guys?&quot;. They Said Yeah Sure! =)<br /> <br /> We are playing together for more than 5 years, working in a storyteller rotation system. There are a few players that are transitory (can't play all the games due work or family) but a few are fixed (yeap, I'm one of those). We are only playing Ex3, we only use Ex1 and Ex2 to get some lore or inspiration. The new combat rules just works for us... it can be little lengthy, but we have a blast of fun stunting and doing crazy shit.<br /> <br /> We already played with all the released exalts for Ex3... (Solar, Lunar, DB, Exigent, Apocryphal and we need to start a game with Sidereal). All games are weekly based. We play 2 or 3 times a week (different campaigns)! We kinda are addicted to Exalted.<br /> <br /> <b>Right Now:</b><br /> We are playing a Solar game in HarbourHead (I'm a Player)<br /> We are playing a Exigent/Apocryphal game in far NorthEast in a huge Lost First Age Prision. (I'm a Player)<br /> We are playing a Lunar game in the Burning Sands and the Skari Tribes (I'm the StoryTeller)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gonzo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1503979-how-do-you-play-exalted?p=1503991#post1503991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Last time I tried, I played with some new friends whose previous rpg experience was mainly 5e... It was almost impossible to make them understand the rules of Essence which were supposedly easier to get. They simply couldn't grasp the concept of two types of attacks. A total mess... My old Exalted table is disbanded, and I can't help but feel that the game in its current state is dead. News about new exalts getting their Kickstarter aren't exciting anymore. I kinda think &quot;damn.. six more years of this horrible horrible edition&quot;. And it's sad...</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> \u200b<br /> Well I guess you had bad luck finding the people with love for the game. We all play thinking we are in a Wuxia movie and we love the intimacy rules for socialize. People that had played and enjoyed WOD or CWOD or narrative games before, are the easiest to get the Exalted playstyle... maybe you should try to find those who like Narrative Games to play with.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gonzo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1503979-how-do-you-play-exalted#post1503979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bonus Question: Do you think Exalted is still worth playing?</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Absolutely YES </b><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you like Alchemicals, please check out my DeviantArt Gallery!! <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> - 5 Magic Materials BeamKlaves and Gyroscopic Chakrans ? OK<br /> - Autochthonia updated World Map? OK<br /> And many more! <a href=\"http://efq.deviantart.com/gallery/48131405/Alchemicals\" target=\"_blank\">http://efq.deviantart.com/gallery/48131405/Alchemicals</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2498-yukiartic","name":"Yukiartic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-02T23:39:08-08:00","id":1504246,"title":"","content":"I am currently playing in an Essence-version reboot of an old Exalted group that went on a years-long hiatus after we were broken under the sheer weight of Ex3. We found that we spent twice as long on systems and dice rolling than actual roleplaying. To be fair, I see several very good ideas in Ex3, the system is simply too cumbersome for me to enjoy, and with the degree of house rules needed for me to enjoy it, I might as well create my own system from scratch.<br /> <br /> So far Essence seems to be have a balance between system and roleplaying far more to the liking of myself and my group. There are good ideas (I like ventures and milestones), a few flaws (I am... <i>not</i> a fan of the attributes, some minor annoyance about a few things that could be smoother, but needed to connect to Ex3) that are easily house ruled into the Void (attributes, I am looking at you!), and given that Ex3 felt like a chore to play, we are pleasantly surprised to find Essence overall enjoyable.<br /> <br /> I was convinced that Exalted was dead for me, and had it not been for Essence I would not consider Exalted worth playing any longer (and wouldn't even be lurking on this forum). The group and I are still in the early stages of our Essence-fueled game, so do not know how Essence works in the long run, but right now I am overall hopeful that Exalted has many good stories for us still.<br /> <br /> I am looking forward to seeing the Essence Companion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Avatar by Raven &amp; Blue Jay.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/663-aleks","name":"Aleks","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar663_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-03T02:25:57-08:00","id":1504251,"title":"","content":"I'm about to restart my game using a hybrid of 2nd and 3rd. 3rd for me has a slightly more interesting map, but was a step back for world lore. I honestly preferred the metaphysics for 2nd of exaltation being a shard a Devine artifact that plugs into the the human soul, that thaumaturgy being the science of Creation that is the foundation of how thier world works. The concept of magictech too cool and useful a concept to pass up but became a concept that was flanderized by the fans in being overly available and how solars suddenly being super optimized beings who had access to the core book and a optimization chart for builds to break the game who had perfect recollection of the first age rather than divinely empowered people blindly grasping at the edges of greatness finding thier way to the world. Plus 3rd edition has the most unusable core book I've ever encountered. It's too big, too scary to bring to the table. Its content should of been cut down and served in multiple sourcebooks. So I'm going to wait for 4th, and finish collecting 2nd.<br /> 2nd maybe easily broken but atleast its manageble to players.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1435-videopete","name":"videopete","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1435_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-03T12:41:38-08:00","id":1504286,"title":"","content":"My preferred method to play any ttrpg is in person with homebrew in place to smooth out what the table sees as issues in the system. I haven't gotten to play exalted in person yet but dnd, dtf, vtm, and pathfinder almost always end up adjusted character creation rules and smoothing out some of the other mechanics. one of the examples of this in dtf your faith rating above 5 each dot gives you a permanent expression of your apocalyptic form, your increased faith bleeds into your actual form and you roll each day to suppress the form trait. its more of a flavor thing than anything else for elder fallen but the table likes it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/359-dezeroth","name":"Dezeroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar359_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"496"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}